refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
arraystream_context_get_params resourcecontext
Retrieves parameter and options information from the stream or context.

&reftitle.parameters;
context
A stream resource or a context resource

&reftitle.changelog;
&Version; &Description;
8.5.0
The notification callable is returned in its normalized form: "STRLEN" is returned as "strlen", and "K::s" or ["K", "S"] as ["K", "s"]. Previously, the stored value was returned unchanged.
8.0.0
Now throws a TypeError if context is not a valid stream or stream context resource. Previously, an E_WARNING was raised and &false; was returned.

  &reftitle.examples;



    stream_context_get_params example


     Basic usage example



<?php
function stream_notification_callback() {}

$ctx = stream_context_create();
$params = array("notification" => "stream_notification_callback");
stream_context_set_params($ctx, $params);

var_dump(stream_context_get_params($ctx));


    &example.outputs;


array(2) {
  ["notification"]=>
  string(28) "stream_notification_callback"
  ["options"]=>
  array(0) {
  }
}
